WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.619
Let's add thirty-five plus twenty-three using a number line.

2
00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:12.466
Break twenty-three into twenty and three. Add the tens first, then the ones.

3
00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:19.526
Start at thirty-five. Move right when adding positive numbers.

4
00:00:20.026 --> 00:00:21.582
Jump ten to forty-five.

5
00:00:22.082 --> 00:00:24.079
Jump ten more to fifty-five.

6
00:00:24.579 --> 00:00:26.436
Two jumps of ten add twenty.

7
00:00:27.758 --> 00:00:33.505
Now zoom in near fifty-five. The spaces on this number line each show one, not ten.

8
00:00:34.842 --> 00:00:37.477
We still need to add three ones.

9
00:00:37.977 --> 00:00:39.695
One jump to fifty-six.

10
00:00:40.195 --> 00:00:41.693
Another to fifty-seven.

11
00:00:42.193 --> 00:00:44.109
And one more to fifty-eight.

12
00:00:46.842 --> 00:00:55.607
Thirty-five plus twenty is fifty-five. Add three more to reach fifty-eight. So thirty-five plus twenty-three equals fifty-eight.

13
00:00:56.925 --> 00:01:04.901
Your turn! What is twenty-six plus twenty-one? Start at twenty-six. Add two tens, then one more. Pause and try it.

14
00:01:08.925 --> 00:01:11.804
Twenty-six plus ten is thirty-six.

15
00:01:12.304 --> 00:01:14.649
Another ten takes us to forty-six.

16
00:01:15.149 --> 00:01:17.193
One more takes us to forty-seven.

17
00:01:17.693 --> 00:01:20.909
Twenty-six plus twenty-one equals forty-seven.
